                <pb facs="0047" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg41"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby, chargé, to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 11.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the Emperor
                    has nominated two commissioners to investigate and report upon the Viceroy Li’s
                    conduct of the Korean business. These commissioners are Weng Tung-ho, president
                    of the board of revenue, and Li Hung-tsao, president of the board of rites.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Denby</hi>, Jr.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
